# Independent criteria, recorded before reading compiler diff

Controlling text: lane docs/spec.md §§2.4–2.5, 3–5, 7; value-types.md; types-joint.md; syntax.md. A type denotes a set of values. Completion adds only the specified deterministic checked equations; inference otherwise stays principal. No new keyword, library identity test, or privileged schema implementation is permissible.

1. Scope/classification: bare lowercase reads ordinary lexical value scope; module qualification is not field access; grouped reads retain meaning; calls remain reserved macros. Pending pattern/header and own-RHS names must not capture an outer name, but entered inner binders may shadow them.
2. Scheduling: expression SCCs/generalization and runtime needs remain unchanged. All type dependencies (also via aliases, inner annotations, effects, pattern heads) order existing groups. Self/SCC/type-expression cycles reject with an actionable chain. Top-level declaration permutation must preserve acceptance and permanent alias meaning.
3. Annotations: fresh instances per occurrence of completed generalized schemes; shared monotypes and nongeneral captures. No extra polymorphism, no flow-known singleton substituted for inferred type, no temporary-bound shape inference. Whole expanded annotations satisfy place rules.
4. Permanent reads: all used parts closed, no invented Never from unfilled variables, no instance chosen to fit a generalized source. At own-source completion, all demands use one snapshot/batch after ordinary checks, original shared variables survive skips, checked equalities preserve all bounds. Earlier-open ownership restrictions hold. Failed batches do not publish misleading aliases or corrupt unrelated recovery.
5. Patterns: head must exist, arity and entire source match, no union alternatives dropped; alias heads linear with only named/tuple paths, exact constant subtrees equal closed source parts; fresh bare binders cannot duplicate each other or types. Unused/no-binder patterns still checked. Reject forbidden shapes. Test partial/open/generalized/skipped/shared arguments separately.
6. Foreign/later reads: whole completed source closed before projection (E0534), no consumer-driven fixing. Exported closed alias works independently of source export. Private nominal types cannot leak via alias or annotations, including alias-only modules.
7. Tooling/runtime: --types preserves principal scheme/invariant variables; queries give correct source/binder targets and usable unrelated results after errors; package interfaces serialize closed structural bodies with canonical nominal/formal identities, stable under private-source renames and sensitive to real type changes. Runtime type tests expand aliases fully, with unchanged execution for type-only dependencies. Try runtime counterexamples at opt 0 and 2.
8. Scale: cycles terminate, alias/dependency chains do not silently turn into holes, ordinary checking does not suffer substantial slowdown.
9. Motivation: ordinary imported Schema/Codec builder and local extraction require no compiler library rule; test nominal scalar/tuple payload now, record payload is T3's gate.

Hard cases to run: value/alias cycles; mutually recursive top-level functions and forbidden type edges; local and reserved-name shadowing; generalized identity and invariant source; unresolved weak source; mismatches/unions/nested/partial/exact patterns; duplicate binders; open and closed foreign sources; declaration order permutations; exports/private nominal/alias-only modules; bad alias plus independent errors; runtime alias type tests and local sharing; package identity and LSP hover/definition/outline/recovery; long dependency chains.

Wording to scrutinize: §4.3 'After source completion' versus own-source completion for skips; §4.7 local inferred structural shape versus simplified completed schemes. Designs distinguish these explicitly.
